  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When an avatar with a sender contact loads, and the sender is immediately in contact with a receiver, sometimes the receiver does not register the contact. This seems to happen more often on the non-local clone of the receiving avatar.\nRepro case:\n1. Have player A load avatar avtr_5e7422c8-ffaa-45a6-8f2a-bcbcd0bb939c (receiver)\n2. Have player B load avatar avtr_b45d3ce7-fd46-41bf-810a-5f91e798a831 (sender)\n3. Initially, the cube above player A's head will be green for both players, indicating the contact is being received.\n4. Have player B hit rejoin world a few times.\n5. Eventually (after 5-6 times typically?) player B will observe the cube above player A's head to be red, indicating that player A's nonlocal clone is not receiving the contact.\n6. Toggle the sender using the option on player B's expressions menu. The cube will go green, indicating that the contact is now being received.",
